# Drafted by Gemini (side quests batch 1: feast), edited.

~ holly_start
holly_aster [angry]: Dust your boots and listen close, newcomers. Tomorrow is the Founders' feast, and Siv Harga thinks her greasy sausage rolls belong at the high table instead of my spiced harvest loaf.
holly_aster [sly]: Carry this warm loaf to Mayor Somerton and speak well of my crust. And sneak a bite of Siv's pastry first, then tell me true if her suet beats my cinnamon.
* We will help -> holly_accept
* Not now -> END

~ holly_accept
holly_aster [smile]: Bless your honest tongues. Mind you hold the cloth flat so the glaze stays shiny.
quest bread_and_circuses asked
set feast_asked
-> END

~ siv_visit
siv_harga [angry]: Holly Aster sent you sniffing round my chopping block, did she? That woman bakes dry sawdust and calls it sacred custom.
siv_harga [neutral]: Try one of my pork rolls before you judge, fresh from the tin. Better yet, carry a tray up to Mayor Somerton and tell him real meat beats sweet dough.
* Taste a sausage roll -> taste
* Carry a roll to the mayor too -> siv_accept
* Leave -> END

~ taste
Narrator: The pastry flakes at the first bite, rich with sage, black pepper, and clean pork fat. You have to admit it is remarkably good.
siv_harga [smile]: Ha! Your eyes just went wide as saucers, stranger. Tell Holly that when you see her.
set siv_tasted
-> siv_visit

~ siv_accept
siv_harga [smile]: Good on you. Keep the grease paper wrapped tight till you reach Somerton's parlour.
set siv_roll_carried
-> END

~ mayor_judges
wendel_somerton [smile]: Come in, come in, my dear friends! Have you brought the contenders for tomorrow's high table?
Narrator: The mayor samples a crumb of spiced crust and a corner of warm pastry, wiping his chin with a linen napkin.
wendel_somerton [weary]: Oh, dear me, both are splendid, yet tradition demands a single crown dish. Which baker claims your vote?
* Praise Holly's loaf -> praise_holly
* Praise Siv's rolls -> praise_siv
* [Persuasion DC 13] Suggest both be served -> both_ok | both_fail
* Poison Siv's table with a pinch of salt -> sabotage

~ praise_holly
wendel_somerton [smile]: The spiced loaf it is! Sweet grain and dark clove, just as the Old Ways remember.
set feast_winner = "holly"
standing old_ways +1
-> ode

~ praise_siv
wendel_somerton [smile]: The sausage rolls take the honour! Hearty fare from the Patient Lady's pasture.
set feast_winner = "siv"
standing patient_lady +1
-> ode

~ both_ok
wendel_somerton [smile]: By the Oak, what wisdom! Savory meat in the left hand, sweet bread in the right! We shall raise a toast to harmony!
set feast_winner = "both"
standing old_ways +1
standing patient_lady +1
-> ode

~ both_fail
wendel_somerton [sad]: Alas, the Founders' charter allows only one dish to lead the grace. You must choose between them.
-> mayor_judges

~ sabotage
Narrator: While the mayor turns to fetch his goblet, {name} tips a heavy cellar of coarse salt straight into Siv's gravy seam. Siv will never know whose hand ruined the batch.
wendel_somerton [afraid]: Merciful heavens, this meat is brined like an old boot! Holly's spiced loaf wins by default!
set feast_winner = "holly"
set feast_sabotaged
standing patient_lady -1
-> ode

~ ode
Narrator: Lanterns swing above the long trestle tables as Ambrose Quill rises, clearing his throat with terrifying authority.
ambrose_quill [smile]: O blessed feast of Wickermoor, where crumbs fall down to sweep the floor more! May bad meat never make us sicker, nor empty tankards drain the quicker!
Narrator: Dead silence hangs over the taproom for three heartbeats, followed by polite, bewildered clapping.
quest bread_and_circuses done
set feast_done
gold +30
-> END
